R"VG(
# instruction_reasons.vg (H-04's second pass): the reasons the far future's instructions give for each step and each prohibition (instructions.vg's),
# the people's own among them.

# ---- why ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

in.why
  (3) {in.why.l}
  (2) We {in.we.did} there {in.we.when}.
  (1) {in.why.l} {in.why.short}
in.we.did
  sat
  sang
  said goodbye
  ate {food}
  waited for the children
  argued, and made up
  watched {skynight}
  kept {festival}
  were at {pastime}
  told the old stories
in.we.when
  every evening
  at the end of the day
  when it rained
  for a thousand years
  until the very end
  on feast days
  when we could not sleep
  {fut.when.past}
in.why.short
  Trust it.
  Go on.
  You will see.
  It is yours now.
in.why.l (share=0.6)
  It will see you.
  It knows the way.
  It will learn your words; any words will do.
  It remembers us; ask it about us.
  It will show you the rest.
  That is where we sat, at the end of the day.
  Nothing here will hurt you.
  It has been waiting a long time.
  It is warm in the long nights.
  It was the first thing we made here, of {material}, and the last we left running.
  It is clean; it has been clean since the last {festival} we kept.
  We did it every day, like feeding the {herd}, and it did us good.
  It is what the old {people} did, and we kept it.
  It is a small thing, and it matters.
  You will understand why after a while, or you will not, and that is all right.
  We were happiest there.
  The children loved it; we hope you do.
  It is older than any of us were, older than the {tree} outside.
  That is how the place knows you are staying.
  It is how we said goodbye, and how we say welcome.
  The place is kinder to people who do it.
  We left it this way on purpose, with the {colour.holy} cloth on top.
  It does the place good to be used.
  Somebody has to, and now it is you.
  You will like it; we did, after a while.
  The machines expect it, and they have been patient, like the {herd}.
  It is the first thing our children learned, before {fut.game}.
  {proverb}, as our old ones said.
  Nobody told us to; we wanted to.
  It keeps the place awake.
in.why2 (share=0.6)
  They are older than they look.
  We never did, and nothing bad happened.
  There is no need.
  They are not for you, or for us any more.
  They will wake when they are ready.
  It would not hurt you; it would only be confused.
  It stops by itself, and starts again.
  It was ours, and we would like it left.
  We are not sure why; we were told the same.
  Some things are better not known, and this is one, like the old {craft} workshop's secrets.
  It is holding something up.
  We tried once. We were sorry.
  It belongs to someone who is not coming back from {city2}.
  The old {people} sealed it, and we trusted them.
  It is sleeping, and it is very tired.
  It is not dangerous; it is private.
  Leave it to the next ones, as we did.
  It does not want to be found, and we respected that.
  Our children asked the same, and got the same answer.
  The reason is in the records, and the records are long.
  It hums when it is happy. Leave it happy.
  We promised, a long time ago, and the promise stands.
  Nothing will come of it but noise, and the {herd} hate noise.
)VG"
